From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a3xx: soft reset the GPU in hw_init

The GPU's runtime suspend gates its clocks and marks it for hw_init, but
the oxili GDSCs only collapse once every device in the domain has
suspended, and the GPU's SMMU shares it with a 20 ms autosuspend. So a
GPU that suspends and resumes while the SMMU is busy comes back with no
power collapse and whatever state the last session left: hw_init then
reloads the microcode and sends CP_ME_INIT to a core that was never
reset, and the first job after it can hang. Pinning the SMMU on, so the
GDSCs never collapse, makes that happen several times a minute.

kgsl handles this in _adreno_start(): if either GPU regulator (the GX or
CX GDSC) is still enabled, it soft resets the core with RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD
before a3xx_start(). drm only did that in a3xx_recover().

Reset at the start of every hw_init. That covers the same cases kgsl's
check does, a GPU the bootloader left on included, and recovery, which
goes through hw_init too, no longer needs its own reset. After a real
collapse the reset changes nothing. The reset clears the RBBM power
counter devfreq takes its baseline from in msm_gpu_pm_resume(), so take
the baseline again under devfreq's lock; otherwise busy time goes
backwards and trips a WARN.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c	2026-10-15 10:22:01.939459745 +0400
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c	2026-10-15 10:22:14.700401849 +0400
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 
 static void a3xx_dump(struct msm_gpu *gpu);
 static bool a3xx_idle(struct msm_gpu *gpu);
+static u64 a3xx_gpu_busy(struct msm_gpu *gpu, unsigned long *out_sample_rate);
 
 /* CP_SET_CONSTANT's address for a register in the 0x2000 block, as kgsl has it */
 #define CP_REG(reg) ((0x4 << 16) | ((reg) - 0x2000))
@@ -121,6 +122,32 @@
 	return a3xx_idle(gpu);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Reset the core, as kgsl's _adreno_start() does whenever it finds the GPU's
+ * regulators still on. Here the core can come to hw_init without having lost
+ * power: runtime suspend only gates its clocks, and the GDSCs collapse only once
+ * the SMMU, which shares them, has suspended too; recovery never collapses them;
+ * and the bootloader may leave them on. hw_init then reloads the microcode on a
+ * core with its old state, and the first job can hang. After a real collapse the
+ * reset changes nothing.
+ *
+ * The reset also clears the busy counter devfreq samples, and devfreq took its
+ * baseline in msm_gpu_pm_resume(). Take it again under devfreq's lock, so no
+ * sample sees the counter go backwards.
+ */
+static void a3xx_soft_reset(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
+{
+	struct msm_gpu_devfreq *df = &gpu->devfreq;
+	unsigned long sample_rate;
+
+	mutex_lock(&df->lock);
+	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 1);
+	gpu_read(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD);
+	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 0);
+	df->busy_cycles = a3xx_gpu_busy(gpu, &sample_rate);
+	mutex_unlock(&df->lock);
+}
+
 static int a3xx_hw_init(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 {
 	struct adreno_gpu *adreno_gpu = to_adreno_gpu(gpu);
@@ -130,6 +157,8 @@
 
 	DBG("%s", gpu->name);
 
+	a3xx_soft_reset(gpu);
+
 	if (adreno_is_a305(adreno_gpu)) {
 		/* Set up 16 deep read/write request queues: */
 		gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_VBIF_IN_RD_LIM_CONF0, 0x10101010);
@@ -393,9 +422,7 @@
 	if (hang_debug)
 		a3xx_dump(gpu);
 
-	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 1);
-	gpu_read(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD);
-	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 0);
+	/* adreno_recover() ends in hw_init, which resets the core */
 	adreno_recover(gpu);
 }
 
